            <ArticleTitle>Atypical facial pain and orbital cancer.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>338-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A patient complaining of facial pain was found to have primary squamous cell cancer of the orbit. The treatment included surgery and radiotherapy. The patient having this extremely rare disease has been followed up for seven years with no evidence of recurrence.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
